          %h2#idea Idea
          %p There are two different things that one might mean by a “complex supermanifold”, and the term is in fact used for two different notions in the literature (the terminology is a mess!):
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                In the first sense, a complex supermanifold generalizes the notion of a smooth manifold with its sheaf of smooth complex-valued functions, just as an ordinary
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
                is a generalization of an ordinary manifold with its sheaf of smooth real-valued functions. However, considering ordinary smooth manifolds as ringed spaces with either their sheaves of real or complex smooth functions gives two equivalent categories, whereas this is not true in the case of real and complex supermanifolds; the corresponding functor is neither essentially surjective nor fully faithful. (For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                a complex supermanifold in this sense, the underlying reduced manifold
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi red
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{red}
                is
                %strong not
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
                but just a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
                regarded as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+space"} ringed space
                with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
                taken to be the sheaf of
                = succeed "-valued" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℂ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            %li
              %p
                In the second sense, a complex supermanifold is a super(complex manifold), a super-version of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
          %h2#complex complex
          %p
            A
            %strong complex supermanifold
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+space"} ringed space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = (|X|, O_X)
            such that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi O
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_X
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
                of commutative complex
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+algebra"} super algebra
            %li
              %p
                locally
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi O
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_X
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi ℂ
                      %msup
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo •
                      %msup
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mi δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^d) \otimes_{\mathbb{C}} \wedge^\bullet \mathbb{C}^\delta
          %p
            Write
            %span.newWikiWord
              cSDiff
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/cSDiff"} ?
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of complex supermanifolds.
          %p
            %strong Example
            The functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi real
                  %mi vector
                  %mi bundles
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo →
                  %mi SDiff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi : \{real vector bundles\} \to SDiff
            has a complex analogue
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi complex
                    %mi vector
                    %mi bundles
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo →
                    %mi cSDiff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi : \{complex vector bundles\} \to cSDiff
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
            be a complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            of rank
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi E
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} same way
            as a real vector bundle gives rise to a real supermanifold: the structure sheaf is given by sections of the exterior algebra of the dual of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %p
            %strong Remark
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X) := O_X(X)
            does not in general have a
            = succeed "-antilinear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{-} : C^\infty(X) \to C^\infty(X)
            but there does exist a canonical complex conjugation on the quotient
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
            by the ideal of nilpotent sections, which is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi red
                    %mo ;
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X_{red}; \mathbb{C})
          %p
            As for ordinary
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
          %p
            %strong Theorem
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Every complex supermanifold is isomorphic to one of the form
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Π
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi E
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi cSDiff
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ComplexSuperAlg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cSDiff(X,Y) \simeq  ComplexSuperAlg(C^\infty(Y), C^\infty(X)).
          %p
            %strong Remark
            It turns out that a
            = succeed "-super" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi : C^\infty(Y) \to C^\infty(X)
            automatically satisfies
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi red
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi red
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi red
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi red
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_{red}(\overline{f_{red}}) = \overline{\phi_{red}(f_{red})}
          %p
            Define the complex supermanifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi cs
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_{cs}^{d|\delta}
            as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d
            with structure sheaf
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\mapsto C^\infty(U) \otimes_{\mathbb{C}} \wedge^\bullet \mathbb{C}^\delta
          %p
            Then for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            an arbitrary complex supermanifold we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi cs
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi cSDiff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi cs
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ev
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mi j
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi odd
                  %mo ;
                  %mi with
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %mi real
                  %mi in
                  %mi that
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi red
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi red
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{R}_{cs}^{d|\delta}(S)
                  \=
                  cSDiff(S, \mathbb{R}_{cs}^{d|\delta})
                  \=
                  \\{
                  (x_1, \cdots, x_d, \theta_1, \cdots, \theta_{\delta})|
                  x_i \in C^\infty(S)^{ev} ,
                  \\theta_j \in C^\infty(S)^{odd};
                  with x_i real in that \overline{(x_i)_{red}} = (x_i)_{red}
                  \\}
          %p
            %strong Example
          %p For
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi θ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ev
                  %mo ,
                  %mi θ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi odd
                  %mo ;
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mi real
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{R}^{2|1}(S)
                  \=
                  \\{
                  (x,y,\theta) |
                  x,y \in C^\infty(S)^{ev},
                  \\theta \in C^\infty(S)^{odd}; x,y real
                  \\}
          %p we shall write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo ,
                  %mover
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo ,
                  %mi θ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi z
                  %mo ,
                  %mover
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ev
                  %mo ;
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi z
                        %mi red
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi z
                    %mo ¯
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi red
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\simeq \{
                  (z,\bar z, \theta)
                  | z, \bar z \in C^\infty(S)^{ev}; \overline{z_{red}}=(\overline z )_{red}
                  \\}.
